  "result": "The number is computed in `nextIssueNumber`, which returns one more than the largest `issues.number` already stored for that org and project (or 1 if there are none). It is scoped by both `orgId` and `projectId`, so each project starts again at 1. Archived issues are included in the max, so their numbers are never reused.\n\n`createIssue` in the issue service calls it and then passes the result to `insertIssue`. The service only supplies the value; the repository decides it. Checking the per-project issue quota happens just before this in the same function, but it doesn't affect the number.\n\nANSWER: src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts",
